description:
FILED s533c (Opus, 2026-11-04), found by the tail probes of the structured `local` (scratch/s533c/p/tl.pl), PRE-EXISTING (main 0f2db817).

REPRODUCER:
  our ($x, %h) = (1);
  sub f { local $x = 5 }  sub k { local $h{q} = 3 }
  my $v = eval { local $x = 9 };
  my @m = map { local $_ = $_ * 2 } (1, 2);
  print scalar(f()), " ", scalar(k()), " $v @m\n";
perl 5.40.3: 5 3 9 2 4
PCL 0f2db817: " " (undef, undef, undef) and an EMPTY map (the eval / map blocks with a tail `local` declined to the v1 text route, whose open let had an empty body, value NIL).

MECHANISM: v1's `local` text left the scope open and the block remainder inside it; with no remainder the open form's value was NIL.  The embedded-block lowering declined a block whose tail is a declaration it cannot value (a `local` is a Statement::Variable), so those blocks took v1's route.

FIX (s533c): the structured `local` plan carries the target's VALUE for the unmodified solo-scalar and single-element shapes; when the statement is the last of a block whose value is used (tail context defined, nothing after it), that value is the innermost form.  A list local's value was already its list assignment's.  An embedded block's tail `local` now lowers structurally (Parser2::_tail_block_stmt_ok); a STRING eval ending in a local keeps its refusal ("trailing declaration has no value") -- not widened here.  Guard: Pl/t/local-stmt-01.t (the #4443 row).

RESIDUE (not this task): `eval { local $1 = 1 }` does not die "Modification of a read-only value attempted" (base and tree alike).


